2 DATE 27 AUG 1780
2 PLAC Gresse, Mecklenburg, Deutschland
2 ADDR
1 BAPM
2 DATE 29 AUG 1780
2 PLAC Gresse, Mecklenburg, Deutschland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 NOV 1870
2 PLAC Lyk, Ostpreußen
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Pastor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.schliemann-museum.de/raum-1/schliemanns-eltern-und-geschwister/
2 CONT
2 CONT SCHLIEMANN'S PARENTS AND SIBLINGS
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich's father, '''E r n s t Johann Adolph Schliemann, born in 1780 in Gresse (Mecklenburg), had been a Protestant pastor since 1814 in the small country town of Neubukow, near the Baltic Sea.''' The family tree of the family c
2 CONC an be traced since the beginning of the 17th century in Wismar and on the island of Poel.
2 CONT Ernst Schliemann had attended the grammar school in Altona and had become a teacher there, at the gates of Hamburg. In the interest of a secure supply, he had taken up the study of theology in Halle/Saale. After this degree, he be
2 CONC came deputy rector in Sternberg (Mecklenburg) at the age of 31. Here he met Heinrich's mother, L o u i s e Therese Sophia Bürger, the daughter of the rector, the later mayor of Sternberg. He married the 13 years younger woman in 1
2 CONC 813, and from this marriage, nine children were born. Heinrich was born in 1822 as the fifth child. In 1838, the father married a second time.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Like all or almost all the pastors, my father had nine children and no money..." H.S., America diary (1850/51)
2 CONT
2 CONT (For further details see: Biographical data of parents and siblings and family tree of the family)
