1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emil_Minlos<br/>
2 CONT Minlos was the son of the Lübeck merchant and Assecuradeurs Hans Simon Minlos (born October 13, 1799 in Lübeck, † April 27, 1847 ibid) and his wife Dorothea Adolphine Friederike Sager (born September 2, 1803 in Lübeck as the daugh
2 CONC ter of the owner of the Löwen pharmacy, Adolf Christoph Sager).<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT We don't know anything about him, apart from a few legends in my family, DNA tests we have done and the fact that he's mentioned by Diego Roselli in:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Historia de 100 ciudades.
2 CONT =
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a German Businessman and was supposed to be born in 1828.
2 CONT He had an affair with Rosa Arango, my great grandmother, 13 years older than him and who had his child in 1852. Emil had disappeared by the time the child came to the world and she called him: Jose Arango. Maria Arango died in 186
2 CONC 0.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT August Adof Emil Minlos Sager. Comerciante Aleman que llego por 1848 a Maracaibo como empleado de la firma Schmilinsky & Montovio. Luego fue Consul (1859-64) de los Estados Alemanes en Maracaibo.
