1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Heinrich Schliemann''' (1822-1890) was a German businessman and a pioneer in the field of archaeology. He was an advocate of the historicity of places mentioned in the works of Homer. Schliemann was an archaeolo
2 CONC gical excavator of Hissarlik, now presumed to be the site of Troy, along with the Mycenaean sites Mycenae and Tiryns. His work lent weight to the idea that Homer's Iliad and Virgil's Aeneid reflect historical events. Schliemann's 
2 CONC excavation of nine levels of archaeological remains with dynamite has been criticized as destructive of significant historical artifacts, including the level that is believed to be the historical Troy. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wi
2 CONC ki/Heinrich_Schliemann Wikipedia EN]
2 CONT ----
