1 NAME Edith-Marie /Lehmann-von Schreiber/
2 GIVN Edith-Marie
2 SURN Lehmann-von Schreiber
2 _MARNM Lehmann-von Schreiber
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 DEC 1912
2 ADDR
3 CITY St.Petersburg
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2005
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00646881&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Edith-Marie von Schreiber was born on 27 December 1912 in St. Petersburg, Russia, daughter of Georg von Schreiber and Adelaide Frohne. In 1914 the beginning of World War One, with her mother and sister and brothers, she 
2 CONC escaped from Russia and went to Lübeck. In Lübeck from 1918 till 1930 she was educated at the Lyceum. After leaving a college at the Foundation Finn in Estland, she went to her uncle Dr. Konrad Lehman as a domestic. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 17 December 1936 in Oldeani, Tanganyika (now Tanzania), Edith-Marie married Kuno Asschenfeldt, son of Gustav Asschenfeldt and Margot Lütgens. They became the parents of five sons. In 1940 at the outbreak of World War Two their 
2 CONC property was confiscated and were forcibly returned to Germany and they went to live in Hamburg. When Mecklenburg was invaded by the Russians she became a refugee for the third time. With her five children she went to Hamburg and 
2 CONC was taken in by her uncle Dr. Konrad Lehmann. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 20 March 1946 in Hamburg Edith-Marie was adopted by Dr. Konrad Lehmann and his wife Elsa Frohne and since then her surname was Lehmann-von Schreiber. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After her husband retired, in 1972 they went to live in Gudow.
