0 @I6000000002764690079@ INDI
1 NAME Ian Meredith /Hughes/
2 GIVN Ian Meredith
2 _MARNM Hughes
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 JAN 1940
2 ADDR
3 CITY Birmingham
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JAN 2012
2 PLAC Norfolk and Norwich University Hospital Colney 
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU research game warden
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} wrote book: “Black Moon, Jade Sea”
2 CONT
2 CONT I was born in a house on the Hagley Road on the outskirts of Birmingham, England's second largest city after London, on the third, January 1940. It was six months into the 2nd World War and my father was at sea as a lieutenant in 
2 CONC the Royal Navy Volunteer Reserve. He was on the Russian Convoys; the blockade-running convoys across the North Sea to Murmansk and Archangel. I would not see him until I was three years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT Back in Birmingham, my mother had become an ambulance driver. In the summer of 1940, the first of the German Air Raids began, and Birmingham along with Coventry in England's industrial heartland were the first British cities to be
2 CONC  bombed. As luck would have it, our house received a direct hit by an incendiary bomb and went up in flames. That incendiary crashed through the roof and on through my cot before exploding and burning the house to the ground. Only
2 CONC  minutes before, on hearing the air-raid sirens, my mother and my grandmother had taken me out of my cot and brought me downstairs to the stairwell - the safest place in the house. That, apparently, was how close it was!
2 CONT
2 CONT After this, my mother and grandmother were evacuated to the farm - Wackley Lodge - of a relative. The farm was near a place called Whitchurch in Shropshire. I vaguely remember various incidents there: shooting foxes on a tractor w
2 CONC ith a farmhand at night, bringing in the harvest, learning to ride a tricycle, being charged by a herd of horses...
2 CONT
2 CONT The next thing I remember was being met off the train by my father - a complete stranger to me -  at a place called Llanbedr in North Wales. It was the dead of night and pouring with rain, and we  ended up in an empty and enormous
2 CONC  Victorian house called Bryn Artro. This was to be my home for nearly a quarter of a century!
2 CONT
2 CONT That more or less covers my early years before I started school. The war was by now over and my father had left the navy. My sister, Ann, had just been born. Everything was very strange. 
