1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Volontør Kadet i Søetaten, deltog 1753 i den marokanske Ekspedition ombord paa Fregatten Falster, med hvilken har 3. Juni 1753 sprang i Luften paa Saffias Rhed, over ham lod Faderen opsætte et Epitafium i Allested 
2 CONC Kirke. 
2 CONT
2 CONT For an account of the conflict that led up to the loss of the frigate Falster see:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.milhist.dk/vaaben/vands/fregatten_falster/falster.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT In the account it says:
2 CONT
2 CONT "At the fire the following men were lost: Second commander lieutenant Suhm, lieutenant baron Christian Carl Liliencrone and Morten Hirschnack, cadet Konrad Bruun, 3 lieutenant of the Marines together with 125 petty officers and se
2 CONC amen. 23 seamen and soldiers survived, by swimming to a small deserted rocky island. These miserable, naked and wounded men were soon taken as slaves."
