1 OCCU Opretter Grevskabet Christiansholm (16-04-1734)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Emerentia von Levetzau was 23 years younger than her husband Johan Otto Raben, and when he died in 1719, she was a very capable woman of 50 years. She owned a couple of other estates, namely  Bremersvold and Egholm. In 1
2 CONC 725 she bought the castle Aalholm and the properties belonging to it, and Bramslökke from King Frederik the 4th.In 1728 she also bought Kjærstrup. In 1734 she founded the estate of Christiansholm for her grandson (son's son) Chris
2 CONC tian Raben. When he was only 9 years old he became Count, and he received a good education and traveled all over Europe. His grandmother ruled the estate with a firm and capable hand. She died 11 Feb 1746 in Aalholm Castle and is 
2 CONC buried in Nysted Church. But Count Christian Raben died in 1750, at the young age of 25, without ever having been married; so his brother Otto Ludwig Raben became Count. [FN::FN]see Aalholm Castle. Also see biography under Otto Lu
2 CONC dwig Raben. Emerentia von Levetzau had a daughter from her first marriage, Charlotte Amalie born 1688. She was married in 1703 to Georg Fredrik von Haxthausen - born 1665 - died 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT INDIVIDUAL_NOTE The information copied from" Danish Nobility" at the Library in Copenhagen by Bernice Raedel in 1956.
